# Sanitized Wazuh Windows Agent Configuration Example

This is a documentation example based on the lab configuration. It is not a backup of the original configuration file.

```xml
<ossec_config>

  <client>
    <server>
      <address>WAZUH_MANAGER_IP</address>
      <port>1514</port>
      <protocol>tcp</protocol>
    </server>
  </client>

  <syscheck>
    <disabled>no</disabled>
    <directories realtime="yes">C:\Wazuh-FIM-Test</directories>
  </syscheck>

</ossec_config>
```

## Configuration notes

- `WAZUH_MANAGER_IP` is a placeholder. Replace it with the manager address only when adapting the example to another lab.
- The agent communicates with the Wazuh Manager over TCP port `1514`.
- File Integrity Monitoring is enabled for the dedicated test directory.
- Real-time monitoring is enabled for the configured directory.

**Security:** This example intentionally excludes credentials, certificates, private keys, and enrollment secrets.